### Description

In our system, we need to synchronize passwords between Keycloak and other systems. This requires handling password updates and resets in the following scenarios:

User password update or reset
Admin-initiated password reset
For user password updates and resets, we can retrieve the password using this.session.getContext().getHttpRequest().getDecodedFormParameters(); with the following event types:

EventType.UPDATE_CREDENTIAL
EventType.RESET_PASSWORD

However, when an admin resets a user's password, the password cannot be accessed through this.session.getContext().getHttpRequest().getDecodedFormParameters(); via AdminEvent.

The reason for this is that admin-initiated password resets use JSON Body instead of form parameters.

Currently, QuarkusHttpRequest : HttpRequest does not provide a function to retrieve the JSON Body.


I request a feature to retrieve the body using getBody in the HttpRequest function.

I think the code might look like this:
```java
public final class QuarkusHttpRequest implements HttpRequest {
...
   @Override
    public String getBody() {
        if (context == null) return null;
        try {
            InputStream inputStream = context.getInputStream();
            if (inputStream == null)
                return null;
            return new String(inputStream.readAllBytes(), StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to read the request body", e);
        }
    }
}
```

