### Description

Problem:
* Clustered Keycloak, 26.6.4
* Custom event listener sends events (`UPDATE_CREDENTIAL` etc..) to e.g. a Kafka topic (sending logic is done in `enlistAfterCompletion`)
* External service consuming the Kafka messages makes a request to Keycloak to retrieve current user data

Right now, Keycloak registers the cache invalidation and the event listener work both as `afterCompletion`, so it can happen that the event listener sends an event to Kafka _before_ Keycloak invalidates the cache of the user. When the external service retrieves the user data, it might reach any of the Keycloak nodes that have a stale cache entry.

### Value Proposition

Support the semantics that when the work of an event listener executes, it is guaranteed that the whole Keycloak cluster has the up to date view of the user.

### Goals

Provide mechanism to order event listener work _after_ user cache invalidation

### Non-Goals

/

### Discussion

_No response_

### Notes

As a workaround, I'm calling `UserCache#evict` before sending the event to the Kafka topic:

```
public class KafkaEventListenerProvider implements EventListenerProvider {

  private final KeycloakSessionFactory sessionFactory;
  private final EventListenerTransaction tx = new EventListenerTransaction(null, this::sendToKafka);

  KafkaEventListenerProvider(KeycloakSession session) {
    this.sessionFactory = session.getKeycloakSessionFactory();
    session.getTransactionManager().enlistAfterCompletion(tx);
  }

  @Override
  public void onEvent(Event event) {
    tx.addEvent(event);
  }

  private void sendToKafka(Event event) {
    evictUserFromCache(event.getRealmId(), event.getUserId());

    // send event to kafka...
  }

  private void evictUserFromCache(String realmId, String userId) {
    if (realmId == null || userId == null) {
      return;
    }
